    pr_ref:  # 185b
    description: "MEASURED CONSEQUENCE, NOT A STYLE COMPLAINT. _get_or_run_analysis is the single\nchokepoint through which ten commands auto-run an analysis on a cache miss:\nslice, search, routes, explain, symbols, io_boundaries, verify_claims,\ntest_coverage, repeat_finder, dead_code_maybe. It calls\n\n    run_survey(repo_root=..., out_path=None, progress=...)\n\nwith NO side-emission flags, so every survey default applies. cmd_survey passes its\nown flags and is unaffected.\n\nThe result is that a caller who typed `slice --files` gets survey's full side-output\nbill. One such invocation on this monorepo — whose question was \"which test files\ndepend on these 2 source files\", answer: 9 files — wrote a 203 MB survey.json, three\ntier previews and 16 handler slices, 204 MB across 20 artifacts. _handle_files_mode\nreads only nodes and edges (Symbol.path, Symbol.id, Edge.src, Edge.dst); it touches\nnothing from sketch_precomputed, entrypoints, metrics, supply_chain_summary, the tier\nfiles or the handler slices.\n\nWHAT IT COSTS, measured (scripts/measure-survey-phase-split.py, --lean arm):\ndeclining sketch fan-out + handler slices + sketch pre-computation on the same tree\ntakes a cold run 517.7s -> 455.0s. So the side-output family is 62.7s, about 12% of\nthe pre-fix wall clock, and roughly 28% of the 220.0s that remains after the WI-balaf\nfix. Not the headline number — that was the fingerprint quadratic — but no longer\nnoise either.\n\nTWO FACTS THAT BOUND THE OPTIONS:\n 1. Cache discovery keys on survey.json ALONE (_discover_input_file ->\n    find_survey_in_dir). The tier files and slice dir are separate artifacts, so\n    declining them cannot break a later cache hit.\n 2. sketch reads sketch_precomputed behind `\"sketch_precomputed\" in cached_results\n    and ... is not None` guards at all four sites, so its absence degrades to\n    recomputing live rather than to wrong output. Skipping it is safe but shifts cost\n    onto a later `sketch` run on the same tree.\n\nWHY THIS IS FILED RATHER THAN FIXED. The owner ruled on the adjacent surface in\nWI-pijal (2026-05-04): \"don't jettison any of those files -- they're earning their\nplace; the friction is purely awareness\", and WI-pijal was narrowed to help-text only\nwith \"behavior change of any kind\" explicitly out of scope. That ruling was about\nexplicit `run --out`, where the user typed the verb. The implicit path is arguably a\ndifferent case — nobody typed `survey`, and the ten callers cannot pass flags — but\n\"arguably different from an explicit owner ruling\" is exactly the shape that should be\nasked rather than assumed.\n\nTHE QUESTION: should the implicit auto-analysis decline side outputs its caller does\nnot read?\n\n  Option A -- decline the separate ARTIFACTS only (tier previews + handler slices),\n    keep sketch_precomputed. Safe by fact 1: the cached map is byte-for-byte the same\n    map, only the uninvited extra files stop appearing. Buys the smaller share.\n  Option B -- A, plus skip sketch pre-computation. Buys the larger share (it is the\n    bulk of the 62.7s: mention-centrality 27.3s + config-info 15.4s), at the cost of\n    a later `sketch` recomputing. Changes what the cached survey.json CONTAINS, which\n    is the part worth a human decision.\n  Option C -- leave it. The files are cheap now relative to the whole run, and\n    WI-pijal's steer extends to this path too.\n\nNo PR proposed. Awaiting triage."  # 185b
    fields: {}  # 185b
